{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1548014-werewolves-the-safety-of-consuming-chocolate","id":1548014,"title":"Werewolves & The Safety of Consuming Chocolate","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-28T22:46:50-08:00","id":1548014,"title":"Werewolves & The Safety of Consuming Chocolate","content":"A more light-hearted subject, especially for werewolves with a sweet tooth before their First Change.<br /> <br /> Chocolate is toxic to Canines.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are Canines.<br /> <br /> Would it therefore be dangerous for them to eat chocolate as humans then transform into their canine forms before it is fully digested, I wonder? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-29T03:50:33-08:00","id":1548018,"title":"","content":"The correct answer is, of course, \u201cOnly when it\u2019s funny\u201d.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-29T03:59:08-08:00","id":1548021,"title":"","content":"Correction: only when the Games Master is running a scenario coincidentally resembling, but legally-distinct from, CHARLIE AND THE CHOCOLATE FACTORY.<br /> <br /> Points will be deducted if lazy GMs make Wonka\u2019s (I mean \u2018Honeycutt\u2019s\u2019) Chocolate Factory a Pentex subsidiary, rather than the life\u2019s work of a deeply odd Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-29T04:47:06-08:00","id":1548023,"title":"","content":"I went into some detail in the CofD version of this thread already. But to put a spin on this:<br /> <br /> It matters on the Breed. Lupus werewolves don't regenerate supernaturally fast in their wolf forms, so they're be less resistant to toxins than a homid that ate something toxic and then shifting to their wolf form. Though, again, it's worth remember that wolves are, on average, considerably heavier than dogs, and as such are going to have a much higher tolerance for theobromine poisoning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-29T13:39:45-08:00","id":1548032,"title":"","content":"Also, unless you're downing baker's chocolate or dark chocolate, the effective dose is going to be about one half to one quarter what it might seem, as milk chocolate is ~25% cacao and ~75% ludicrous amounts of sugar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-29T14:43:18-08:00","id":1548036,"title":"","content":"To provide a &quot;serious&quot; answer, chocolate would be a type of poison for canids, and we should use the rules for poison. <br /> <br /> First, poisons tend to only work in someone's breed form. Humans can ingest chocolate just fine, so no bad effects there even if they change to lupus or eat it while in lupus. I would say it should be the same for metis as well. So only lupus breed Garou who are in lupus form could be affected by the poison.<br /> <br /> Second, what type of poison should it be for lupus breed in lupus form? I would say it is a very weak form of poison. Chocolate can kill canids, but it is generally very rare that they do. It is much more usual that they become nauseous with later vomiting and diarrhea after a few hours. The W20 description for Weak Poison suggests one to three levels of lethal damage per scene, and if they Garou does not regenerate subtract one from all dice pools until damage is healed. A Garou in a regenerating form (non-breed), &quot;burns through the poison's effects in seconds and suffers no ill effects.&quot; (That is why a homid in lupus form could eat chocolate just fine.)<br /> .<br /> Third, the Gift Resist Toxin would obviously make you immune to that.<br /> <br /> The same would apply to any other popular human good that is not good for canids like alcohol, garlic, grapes/raisins, and onions.<br /> <br /> So for even a strict ST who would enforce such things, the only Garou who could suffer from it are lupus breed who eat it in lupus form and do not change to another form and do not have Resist Toxin or some other Gift. Not something to worry about it, IMO. A lupus who eats chocolate for the first time in breed form probably gets an upset stomach, gets over it, and never eats it again.<br /> <br /> If they have a sweet tooth, they probably eat something else that is sugary that doesn't affect them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}